{"id":"e5a798f4ea2472f5","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-trapping.md","title":"Generic-Extension Trapping Property","display":"df-trapping — Generic-Extension Trapping Property","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-trapping","aliases":["58-df-trapping"],"display":"df-trapping — Generic-Extension Trapping Property","depends_on":["[[58-df-forcing]]","[[58-df-poset]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-trapping"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-trapping</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-trapping — Generic-Extension Trapping Property"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"d06ac5a66d69d291\" href=\"?note=d06ac5a66d69d291\" title=\"58-df-forcing\">58-df-forcing</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d3f859dbdd37f018\" href=\"?note=d3f859dbdd37f018\" title=\"58-df-poset\">58-df-poset</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> is a countable transitive model of the theory <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma\">\\(\\Gamma\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(P,R)\\in M\">\\((P,R)\\in M\\)</span> is a forcing poset.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M[G]_P\">\\(M[G]_P\\)</span> is the generic extension notation from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d06ac5a66d69d291\" href=\"?note=d06ac5a66d69d291\" title=\"58-df-forcing\">58-df-forcing</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CTM}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{CTM}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Poset}\">\\(\\mathrm{Poset}\\)</span> are supplied by the dependencies.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NontrivialPoset}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{NontrivialPoset}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Trap}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Trap}_S\\)</span> are defined here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}trapping\\text{-}nontrivial}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{NontrivialPoset}_S(Q,S)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Poset}(Q,S)\\land\\exists q_0,q_1\\in Q\\;\\neg\\exists r\\in Q\\;(\n\\langle r,q_0\\rangle\\in S\\land\\langle r,q_1\\rangle\\in S)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}trapping\\text{-}nontrivial}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{NontrivialPoset}_S(Q,S)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Poset}(Q,S)\\land\\exists q_0,q_1\\in Q\\;\\neg\\exists r\\in Q\\;(\n\\langle r,q_0\\rangle\\in S\\land\\langle r,q_1\\rangle\\in S)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}trapping}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Trap}_S(P,R,M,\\Gamma)\\leftrightarrow\n\\left[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\\land\\langle P,R\\rangle\\in M\\land\\mathrm{Poset}(P,R)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall G\\;\\left(\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(G,M,P,R)\\to\n\\exists Q,S\\in M[G]_P\\;\\left[\\mathrm{NontrivialPoset}_S(Q,S)\\right.\\right.\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad{}\\left.\\left.\\land\\forall H\\;\\left(\n\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(H,M[G]_P,Q,S)\\to\n\\exists K\\;\\left(\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(K,M,P,R)\\land\nM[G]_P[H]_Q=M[K]_P\\right)\\right)\\right]\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}trapping}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Trap}_S(P,R,M,\\Gamma)\\leftrightarrow\n\\left[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\\land\\langle P,R\\rangle\\in M\\land\\mathrm{Poset}(P,R)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall G\\;\\left(\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(G,M,P,R)\\to\n\\exists Q,S\\in M[G]_P\\;\\left[\\mathrm{NontrivialPoset}_S(Q,S)\\right.\\right.\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad{}\\left.\\left.\\land\\forall H\\;\\left(\n\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(H,M[G]_P,Q,S)\\to\n\\exists K\\;\\left(\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(K,M,P,R)\\land\nM[G]_P[H]_Q=M[K]_P\\right)\\right)\\right]\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This file uses “trapping” as explicit local vocabulary for a nontrivial two-step absorption property: after forcing with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\">\\(P\\)</span>, a further nontrivial generic extension can still be represented as a single <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\">\\(P\\)</span>-generic extension of the original ground.</li>\n<li>The former clause merely required the original ground to be contained in a later extension, which is automatic and made every forcing notion satisfy the predicate.</li>\n<li>No implication from resurrection axioms is asserted without a separately formalized theorem and hypotheses.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-forcing","status":"resolved","id":"d06ac5a66d69d291","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-forcing]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-poset","status":"resolved","id":"d3f859dbdd37f018","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-poset]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-forcing","status":"resolved","id":"d06ac5a66d69d291","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$M[G]_P$ is the generic extension notation from [[58-df-forcing]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"M","display":false},{"tex":"\\Gamma","display":false},{"tex":"(P,R)\\in M","display":false},{"tex":"M[G]_P","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CTM}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Poset}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{NontrivialPoset}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Trap}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}trapping\\text{-}nontrivial}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{NontrivialPoset}_S(Q,S)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Poset}(Q,S)\\land\\exists q_0,q_1\\in Q\\;\\neg\\exists r\\in Q\\;(\n\\langle r,q_0\\rangle\\in S\\land\\langle r,q_1\\rangle\\in S)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}trapping}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Trap}_S(P,R,M,\\Gamma)\\leftrightarrow\n\\left[\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\\land\\langle P,R\\rangle\\in M\\land\\mathrm{Poset}(P,R)\\\\\n&{}\\land\\forall G\\;\\left(\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(G,M,P,R)\\to\n\\exists Q,S\\in M[G]_P\\;\\left[\\mathrm{NontrivialPoset}_S(Q,S)\\right.\\right.\\\\\n&\\qquad{}\\left.\\left.\\land\\forall H\\;\\left(\n\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(H,M[G]_P,Q,S)\\to\n\\exists K\\;\\left(\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(K,M,P,R)\\land\nM[G]_P[H]_Q=M[K]_P\\right)\\right)\\right]\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\\right]","display":true},{"tex":"P","display":false},{"tex":"P","display":false}],"bytes":1975,"backlinks":[{"id":"a11585cba9c21cfd","anchor":"ref-375","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-df-trapping]]"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1322","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-trapping.md|58-df-trapping]]（batch15）"}],"outgoing":["d06ac5a66d69d291","d3f859dbdd37f018"]}